# probes/deduction.cpp must compile with the generated code's flags and run
# under GCC, Clang and the host compiler. Its exit status reports two C++23
# library features: 2 * (std::move_only_function available) + (std::ranges::to
# available). 0, as measured on libstdc++ 13.3, is what the native backend
# assumes: it relies on neither. A non-zero exit means those assumptions must
# be revisited before the change is accepted.
# Native.cmake fails configuration without both toolchains, so no RUN
# line here is ever skipped.
#
# RUN: %gxx -std=c++20 %S/../../../probes/deduction.cpp -o %t.gxx && %t.gxx
# RUN: %clangxx -std=c++20 %S/../../../probes/deduction.cpp -o %t.clangxx && %t.clangxx
# RUN: %host_cxx -std=c++20 -pedantic -Wall -Wextra -Werror -Wconversion %S/../../../probes/deduction.cpp -o %t.host && %t.host
